00:21:24.330 --> 00:21:27.270
If I know Reeves, he'll run right to Addison.

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:29.100
Well, then what?

00:21:29.770 --> 00:21:29.970
Then...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:31.320
your troubles will be over.

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:44.270
Listen, what do you mean Post doesn't want the house?

00:21:44.410 --> 00:21:45.210
He bought it, didn't he?

00:21:46.000 --> 00:21:48.370
Sure, but he wants to make you give him back the money

00:21:48.370 --> 00:21:49.310
without asking for it.

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:49.990
That's ridiculous.

00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:51.110
The man's out of his mind.

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.770
That's exactly what he wants you to believe.

00:21:53.670 --> 00:21:55.350
That's why he told me the horse talks.

00:21:55.690 --> 00:21:55.870
Right.

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:57.210
Don't you understand?

00:21:57.610 --> 00:21:59.310
It's the oldest trick in the real estate game.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.710
He wants to make us think he's got a screw loose up here.

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:04.870
That way you'll try to get him out of the neighborhood.

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:06.910
I see. Well, he'll never get away with it.

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:10.520
Mr. Addison, you tried to settle this house for a long time.

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:12.250
There were no takers at your price.

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.320
You leave it to me, Reeves.

00:22:14.800 --> 00:22:16.440
I know how to handle post.

00:22:17.620 --> 00:22:18.920
Carol, will you come downstairs?

00:22:21.240 --> 00:22:22.340
Honey, I'll make your lunch.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:23.770
I'm not hungry.

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:26.070
Honey, there's nothing to worry about.

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:29.110
Somebody just told me how to straighten out this whole mess.

00:22:31.760 --> 00:22:33.000
Maybe you'd better stay upstairs.

00:22:34.700 --> 00:22:39.650
Mr. Anderson?

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:40.430
Hello, Wilbur.

00:22:40.530 --> 00:22:41.570
I want you to come on in. Sit down.

00:22:41.770 --> 00:22:42.910
Thank you. Thank you very much.

00:22:42.930 --> 00:22:43.890
A pleasant surprise.

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:50.580
My horse just told me a very funny story.

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:52.000
Funniest one I've heard in years.

00:22:52.600 --> 00:22:53.760
I'm still laughing about it.

00:22:54.320 --> 00:22:55.560
Well, let me hear it.

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:59.050
Well, these two fellows are at a bar, you see.

00:22:59.310 --> 00:22:59.970
And one of them said...

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:08.500
give me four martinis I know that joke yeah my dog told it to me well your

00:23:08.500 --> 00:23:14.380
horse told it to my cat my cat told it to my dog and my dog told it to me I like

00:23:14.380 --> 00:23:21.140
the way things get around Wilbur if I cut two thousand dollars off the price of

00:23:21.140 --> 00:23:27.690
the house will that make you stay too is it a deal it's a deal now Wilbur does

00:23:27.690 --> 00:23:28.490
Is your horse talk?

00:23:28.880 --> 00:23:29.200
No.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:30.700
Is your dog talk?

00:23:30.840 --> 00:23:30.960
No.

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:31.900
Your cat?

00:23:32.140 --> 00:23:32.440
Mm-mm.

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:35.580
You know, for a minute, I was a little worried about you.

00:23:35.800 --> 00:23:37.280
I was not worried about you.

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:40.930
Oh, and by the way, the party is not canceled.

00:23:41.090 --> 00:23:42.310
I'm expecting you and your wife.

00:23:42.510 --> 00:23:43.330
Oh, just a minute.

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:50.890
Honey, Mr. Addison's here.

00:23:50.970 --> 00:23:52.450
He's inviting us to the party tonight.

00:23:56.790 --> 00:23:58.670
Not only that, he likes us so much,

00:23:58.770 --> 00:23:59.810
he's knocked $2,000.

00:24:00.124 --> 00:24:00.964
the price of the house.

00:24:02.236 --> 00:24:04.236
Thank you, Mr. Addison.

00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:05.680
Oh, Wilbur.

00:24:05.680 --> 00:24:06.980
Honey.

00:24:11.868 --> 00:24:13.868
That's how I came in.

00:24:30.828 --> 00:24:31.328
And?

00:24:31.692 --> 00:24:32.192
You sleep?

00:24:32.620 --> 00:24:33.420
Not anymore.

00:24:33.932 --> 00:24:35.932
I don't think everything worked out fine.

00:24:36.396 --> 00:24:38.996
We went to the party, the ladies invited Carol out to lunch.

00:24:39.236 --> 00:24:39.796
Whoa, girl.

00:24:40.588 --> 00:24:40.848
Yeah.

00:24:41.836 --> 00:24:42.436
Good night.

00:24:42.956 --> 00:24:46.956
Well, I haven't finished telling you about Carol.

00:24:47.116 --> 00:24:48.256
Good night, Wilbur.

00:24:51.404 --> 00:24:52.064
Good night.

00:24:58.668 --> 00:24:59.168
people.

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:00.840
Talk.

00:25:00.956 --> 00:25:02.756
Ta-ta-ta-ta.

00:25:51.244 --> 00:25:53.244
in a Filmways television presentation.
